# The two that have never been recorded

`r6e` and `r70` answer, have a slot of their own in the firmware, and have **never been in a preset** — every set so far missed them. There is no data on them at all, which makes them the cheapest thing left to learn something about.

The four word-sized ones ride along for a second chance: `r5d` `r5e` `r5f` `r63` held a flat zero through the rev limiter, full throttle, long overruns and a warm-up to 97 °C, so if they move at all it is under something that ride did not do. `r3e` has read a constant 52 through everything including a full cold start.

## How to capture

An ordinary ride, but reach for the states the last one skipped:

- stop in traffic long enough for the fan to cycle twice;
- a hot restart after ten minutes standing;
- ride with the side stand down and the clutch pulled at a standstill;
- a gear change at low rpm, and one at the limiter;
- if anything ever throws a fault light, that whole ride is worth keeping.

## What counts as a result

Any of the six leaving its usual value for even one sample. Write down what was happening and repeat it — one sample is a hint, twice is a channel.
